1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,310
In 1930,

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:03,620
they started the tallest building in the

3
00:00:03,620 --> 00:00:04,290
world.

4
00:00:05,260 --> 00:00:06,460
410 days later,

5
00:00:06,460 --> 00:00:07,430
it was finished.

6
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:09,450
102 stories.

7
00:00:09,900 --> 00:00:11,830
Here's how you build that fast.

8
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:12,680
Step one:

9
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:13,450
the steel.

10
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,820
Tens of thousands of tons of it,

11
00:00:15,820 --> 00:00:17,720
and no room on the site to pile

12
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:18,430
it up.

13
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,680
So you order it two floors at a

14
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:21,100
time,

15
00:00:21,100 --> 00:00:23,320
and it arrives right when you need it.

16
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:25,540
But now your trucks are jamming one of

17
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:27,280
the busiest streets in the city.

18
00:00:27,280 --> 00:00:29,980
So you run a driveway straight through

19
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:30,560
the building,

20
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:32,710
and unload inside.

21
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:35,180
But every load still has to cross the

22
00:00:35,180 --> 00:00:35,580
floor,

23
00:00:35,580 --> 00:00:37,910
and wheelbarrows are slow.

24
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,580
So you lay railway track inside the

25
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:40,940
building,

26
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:43,170
and roll it across on carts.

27
00:00:43,260 --> 00:00:45,680
But 10 million bricks need somewhere to

28
00:00:45,680 --> 00:00:46,310
go.

29
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:48,520
So you pour them down a chute into

30
00:00:48,520 --> 00:00:49,180
the basement,

31
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,660
and lift them only when a floor is

32
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:52,210
ready.

33
00:00:52,280 --> 00:00:54,170
But steel has to be joined.

34
00:00:54,420 --> 00:00:56,740
So one man heats a rivet until it

35
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:57,280
glows,

36
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:58,590
and throws it.

37
00:00:58,700 --> 00:01:00,710
Another catches it in a can.

38
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:03,540
And they hammer it in before it cools.

39
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,720
But now thousands of men are working

40
00:01:05,720 --> 00:01:07,150
hundreds of feet up,

41
00:01:07,260 --> 00:01:09,130
and lunch is on the ground.

42
00:01:09,600 --> 00:01:11,800
So you put the cafeterias up there with

43
00:01:11,800 --> 00:01:12,220
them.

44
00:01:12,220 --> 00:01:13,110
At the peak,

45
00:01:13,260 --> 00:01:16,880
3,400 people are on the job in a

46
00:01:16,880 --> 00:01:17,830
single day.

47
00:01:18,120 --> 00:01:20,220
And the frame is climbing four and a

48
00:01:20,220 --> 00:01:21,420
half floors a week.

49
00:01:21,420 --> 00:01:24,230
410 days after it started,

50
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,030
it's done.

51
00:01:25,460 --> 00:01:27,490
The tallest building in the world.

52
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:30,240
It opens in 1931,

53
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,050
in the middle of the Great Depression.

54
00:01:33,660 --> 00:01:35,790
Most of the offices sit empty.

55
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,340
New Yorkers call it the Empty State

56
00:01:38,340 --> 00:01:39,130
Building.

57
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,280
They built it faster than they could

58
00:01:41,280 --> 00:01:41,970
fill it.
